    "forensics": "The losing cluster is primarily driven by an overly demanding volume sweep threshold (2.85x) that triggers late entries at the peak of exhaustion spikes, resulting in immediate mean-reversion stop-outs (Trades 1, 2, 3, 4, 6) during the 11:45\u201312:45 IST midday liquidity lull. Furthermore, an unattainable target (1.45%) and delayed breakeven trigger (1.05R) caused profitable intraday moves (Trades 5, 7) to round-trip into fee-dragged net losses or EOD square-offs.",
    "learning": "In Indian NSE large-cap cash equities, volume spikes exceeding 2.5x after 10:15 IST often signal short-term climax exhaustion rather than institutional trend continuation; capturing earlier impulse momentum with a ~2.1x volume filter, tighter initial stops (0.55%), and faster risk-removal (0.85R breakeven trigger) is essential to overcome statutory fee drag on small capital.",
