    "plan_update_summary": "### Cycle #23 Post-Mortem & Parameter Mutation\nForensic analysis of Cycle #23 revealed severe fee drag (\u20b947.23 fees against \u20b9-49.04 Net P&L) and exhaustion whipsaws caused by chasing extreme volume spikes (`min_sweep_vol_multiplier` at 2.85x) and holding for overextended targets (`min_target_pct` at 1.45%). Several trades achieved positive gross excursion before reversing during the midday volume lull or stagnating into EOD square-offs, turning gross wins into net losses after brokerage and STT. For Cycle #24, we are recalibrating the execution engine to enter earlier in the institutional impulse curve by lowering `min_sweep_vol_multiplier` to 2.15x, tightening `min_sl_pct` to 0.55% to cut invalidations faster while maintaining favorable reward-to-risk, reducing `min_target_pct` to a realistic 1.15% intraday expansion, and accelerating `breakeven_trigger_r` to 0.85R to aggressively neutralize transaction cost drag."
